---
title: "reserve flash_loan lifecycle (Current Finance: Reserve)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_amount: assert amount lt cash
    q_check_amount --> q_withdraw: flash_loan_withdraw(amount)
    q_withdraw --> q_create_receipt: ReserveFlashLoan { amount }
    q_create_receipt --> q_return: return (Balance, ReserveFlashLoan)
    q_return --> q_usage: borrower uses funds in same PTB

    q_usage --> q_repay: repay_flash_loan(loan, coin, fee)
    q_repay --> q_unpack: ReserveFlashLoan { amount } = loan
    q_unpack --> q_check_exact: assert coin.value == amount
    q_check_exact --> q_join: underlying_balance.join(coin)
    q_join --> q_check_fee: fee.value == 0?
    q_check_fee --> q_destroy_zero: fee.destroy_zero()
    q_check_fee --> q_add_to_reserve: increase_reserve_only(fee)
    q_destroy_zero --> [*]
    q_add_to_reserve --> q_update_cash: cash += fee, cash_reserve += fee
    q_update_cash --> [*]

    note right of q_withdraw
        INV-001: flash_loan_withdraw bypasses cash_reserve check (can borrow all cash)
        INV-002: Normal borrow_amount enforces cash - cash_reserve gt amount
        INV-003: Flash loan does NOT update debt tracking (no interest on flash loans)
        INV-004: Fee goes entirely to cash_reserve (protocol revenue)
        INV-005: ReserveFlashLoan is consumed on repay (hot potato pattern)
    end note
